# 4 Blocks v2 — Architecture Blueprint

> Reference document for building the next prototype of the sliding-block puzzle game.

## Game Concept
A **2D grid-based sliding-block puzzle**. 4 colored blocks inside a walled arena. Player chooses a direction (WASD) and **all blocks slide simultaneously** in that direction — each block slides until it individually hits a wall or another stopped block. Goal: move all blocks to their target positions.

---

## Architecture Overview

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    subgraph Core
        GM[GameManager\nSingleton]
        LM[LevelManager]
        LD[LevelData\nScriptableObject]
    end

    subgraph Gameplay
        B[Block ×4]
        WA[Walls\nCompositeCollider2D]
        GR[GridSystem]
    end

    subgraph Input
        IA[PlayerInputActions\nNew Input System]
    end

    subgraph UI
        HUD[HUD\nMoves · Level · Restart]
        WS[WinScreen]
    end

    IA --> GM
    GM --> B
    GM --> LM
    LM --> LD
    GM --> GR
    GM --> HUD
    GM --> WS
    B --> WA
    B --> GR
```

---

## Component Specifications

### 1. GameManager (Singleton MonoBehaviour)
**Purpose**: Centralized controller — handles input, game state, block selection.

| Responsibility | Details |
|---|---|
| **Game State** | Enum: `Playing`, `Won`, `Paused` |
| **Input handling** | Reads WASD once per frame, sends to **all blocks** simultaneously |
| **Move tracking** | Increments on each successful slide (one WASD press = one move) |
| **Win check** | After **all blocks** stop, check if all blocks are on targets |
| **Undo system** | Stack of [(allBlockPositions[])](file:///c:/Users/mijot/OneDrive/Documents/unity/4%20Blocks%2000/Assets/PlayerInputActions.cs#265-269) snapshots |
| **Prevents input during slide** | Global `isAnyBlockMoving` check — no new input until all 4 blocks have stopped |

### 2. Block (MonoBehaviour, on each block GameObject)
**Purpose**: Handles sliding movement for one block. Does NOT read input — receives slide commands from GameManager.

| Property / Method | Details |
|---|---|
| `SlideInDirection(Vector2 dir)` | Public method called by GameManager |
| `IsSliding` | Read-only property |
| `OnStopped` event | Fires when block finishes sliding (GameManager listens) |
| `SnapToGrid()` | Rounds position to nearest grid unit |
| `GridPosition` | Returns current snapped `Vector2Int` position |

**Movement approach**: **Grid-based with physics**.
- Use `rb.Cast()` to pre-calculate how far the block can slide
- Use `rb.MovePosition()` or lerp to slide to the target grid cell
- Snap to exact grid on arrival

### 3. GridSystem (MonoBehaviour or static utility)
**Purpose**: Manages the grid coordinate system.

| Method | Details |
|---|---|
| `WorldToGrid(Vector3)` → `Vector2Int` | Converts world position to grid coords |
| `GridToWorld(Vector2Int)` → `Vector3` | Converts grid coords to world position |
| `IsOccupied(Vector2Int)` → `bool` | Checks if a grid cell has a block or wall |
| `GetSlideDestination(Vector2Int start, Vector2 dir)` → `Vector2Int` | Calculates where a block would stop |

### 4. LevelData (ScriptableObject)
**Purpose**: Stores level configuration — reusable, easy to create new levels.

| Field | Type | Details |
|---|---|---|
| `levelName` | `string` | Display name |
| `gridWidth` / `gridHeight` | `int` | Arena dimensions |
| `blockStartPositions` | `Vector2Int[4]` | Where blocks spawn |
| `blockTargetPositions` | `Vector2Int[4]` | Win condition positions |
| `wallPositions` | `Vector2Int[]` | Interior wall cells |

### 5. LevelManager (MonoBehaviour)
**Purpose**: Loads LevelData, spawns blocks and walls, handles level transitions.

### 6. Walls
**Same proven approach as v1:**
- Parent object with `Rigidbody2D` (Static) + `CompositeCollider2D`
- Children: `BoxCollider2D` (CompositeOperation = Merge) + `SpriteRenderer`
- `NoFriction` physics material

---

## Input Setup

### PlayerInputActions (New Input System)
| Action Map | Action | Type | Bindings |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Player** | Move | Value (Vector2) | WASD |
| **Player** | Undo | Button | Z / Ctrl+Z |
| **Player** | Restart | Button | R |

---

## Physics Configuration (Same as v1, proven working)

| Setting | Blocks | Walls |
|---|---|---|
| Body Type | Dynamic | Static |
| Gravity Scale | 0 | N/A |
| Collision Detection | Continuous | Discrete |
| Constraints | Freeze Rotation Z | Freeze Rotation Z |
| Physics Material | NoFriction (friction=0, bounce=0) | NoFriction |
| Collider Size | 0.95 × 0.95 | 1 × 1 |

