## Game Flow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Game Start] --> B[LevelManager loads LevelData]
    B --> C[Spawn Walls + Blocks at start positions]
    C --> D[GameState = Playing]
    D --> E{Player Input}
    E -- WASD --> F{Any block sliding?}
    F -- No --> G[Save positions to undo stack]
    G --> H[All 4 Blocks.SlideInDirection]
    H --> I[Each block slides until hitting wall/block]
    I --> J[Each block: SnapToGrid + OnStopped]
    J --> K{All 4 blocks stopped?}
    K -- No --> J
    K -- Yes --> L[GameManager: moveCount++]
    L --> M{All blocks on targets?}
    M -- Yes --> N[GameState = Won → WinScreen]
    M -- No --> E
    E -- Z --> O[Undo last move - restore all 4 positions]
    E -- R --> P[Restart level]
    F -- Yes --> E
```

---

## Key Differences from v1

| Aspect | v1 (Current) | v2 (New) |
|---|---|---|
| Input handling | Each block reads input independently | GameManager reads once, sends to **all blocks** |
| Movement | Physics velocity-based | Grid-based with position snapping |
| Core mechanic | All move together (but independently processed) | All move together (centrally coordinated by GameManager) |
| Win condition | None | Check target positions after all blocks stop |
| Level data | Hardcoded in scene | ScriptableObject |
| Undo | None | Move history stack (snapshots all 4 positions) |
| File organization | All scripts in root Assets | Organized in subfolders |
